    "description": "Natural Mineral Specimen\nAmethyst and Rose Quartz Crystal Collection\nNatural Stone Clusters and Points\nLargest piece approx. 3.5\" x 3\"; Total weight 1.5 lbs\nUnsigned\nThis diverse collection features a variety of natural mineral specimens, highlighted by a substantial amethyst druzy cluster with a characteristic dark, possibly copper or silicate-rich matrix. The lot includes six individual pieces showcasing different geological formations, including deep violet amethyst clusters, translucent rose quartz, and raw crystal points. The pieces demonstrate a beautiful range of color saturation and crystalline structures, making them excellent examples for geological study or natural home decor.\nFeatures one large amethyst druzy specimen with a distinct teal-colored matrix back\nIncludes 6 individual pieces consisting of amethyst clusters, points, and rose quartz\nTotal combined weight of the specimens is 1.495 lbs (measured on scale)\nLargest cluster measures approximately 3.5 inches in width according to Westcott ruler\nCondition:\nVery good natural condition. These are raw mineral specimens and feature natural inclusions, terminations, and matrix variations inherent to their formation. The crystal points are largely intact with expected minor abrasions consistent with raw extraction. No evidence of artificial dyes or repairs.\nThis is a pre-owned item donated to Goodwill of Northern Michigan.\nPlease see images for further detail and ask any questions you may have before making a bid.\nItems have been tested for power, not function. In some instances we may not have the necessary equipment to test certain electronics therefore all items will be auctioned off AS-IS with no refunds.\nItems in lots are sold as-is, are not eligible for refunds, and may not be individually wrapped.\nPlease contact us before making payment to review combined shipping options.\nPick-Ups\nWe're open Monday - Friday, 8 am - 4 pm. We are closed on weekends and major holidays. For local pickup in Traverse City, please give us 24 hours from time of payment to prepare your order. Thank you!",
